---
import ArticlePage from "../../templates/ArticlePage.astro";
import { fuPilotPage } from "../../content/fu-pilot";

const meta = {
  title: "Privacy notes — FU Digital Journeys",
  description: "Draft privacy and participation principles for the FU Digital Journeys pilot.",
};
---
<ArticlePage
  meta={meta}
  header={fuPilotPage.header}
  footer={fuPilotPage.footer}
  eyebrow="FU Digital Journeys"
  title="Privacy and participant control"
  intro="The pilot is being built around deliberate recording, review before sharing, and data minimisation."
  status="Draft protocol"
>
  <p>
    This page describes the intended handling model while the pilot workflow is still being implemented.
    Before recruitment begins, it should be updated to match the exact Recorder build, storage location,
    retention period, contact details and consent process used by the pilot.
  </p>

  <h2>Recording is deliberate</h2>
  <p>
    A participant should explicitly start and stop each research session. The project is not intended
    to passively instrument FU websites or observe students who did not choose to take part.
  </p>

  <h2>Review comes before contribution</h2>
  <p>
    The intended flow separates recording from sharing. Participants should be able to inspect the
    captured material, remove sensitive or irrelevant parts, and only then decide whether to contribute
    the session to the pilot.
  </p>

  <h2>Collect only what the research needs</h2>
  <p>
    Browser sessions can contain personal or sensitive information in URLs, page content, forms and
    screenshots. The implementation should prefer local filtering and redaction where possible and
    avoid collecting material that is not necessary for journey reconstruction.
  </p>

  <h2>Volunteers are not a representative sample</h2>
  <p>
    Contributed sessions are qualitative examples of experience. The pilot must not present path counts
    as estimates of how frequently the wider FU student population uses a route.
  </p>

  <h2>Before the pilot opens</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Document exactly what Recorder captures in the pilot configuration.</li>
    <li>Document where contributed data is stored and who can access it.</li>
    <li>Define retention and deletion procedures.</li>
    <li>Provide participant information and a documented consent process where required.</li>
    <li>Provide a real project contact and withdrawal route.</li>
  </ul>
</ArticlePage>
